                    "created_at": "1774881598",
                    "text": "AI B2B SaaS startups are now being built by younger founders faster than ever before.\nMany of these teams launch products early, focus on solving niche business problems, and prioritize traction even before turning profitable.\n\nThis reflects a shift in how modern startups are built. Investors today often look beyond early profitability and focus on product-market fit, speed of execution, and the size of the opportunity — especially in fast-growing sectors like AI.\n\nFor founders, the lesson is clear:\nEarly-stage success is less about immediate profits and more about proving demand. Building something useful that people adopt quickly often matters more than perfect financials in the beginning.\n\nDisclaimer: Content is shared for educational, storytelling, and commentary purposes under Fair Use (Section 107).\nWe transform original material with insight and narrative.\nNo ownership claimed on third-party assets; credit given when possible.\nDM for credit or takedown @101xfounders\nReposts, reuploads & AI scraping are prohibited.\n.\n.\nFor more insights and videos like this\nFollow @101xfounders",
